  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{x}={{(\\,4\\,)}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{\u23df}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=4\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-3)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-3.$",
